    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q102-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Identify $\\sec\\theta$, $\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta$ and $\\cot\\theta$ on the diagram.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sec\\theta=OA$, $\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=OB$, $\\cot\\theta=PB$.",
          "worked": "The tangent at $P$ is perpendicular to $OP$. With $OP=1$, the right-triangle ratios give $OA=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$, $OB=\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}$ and $PB=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$.\n\nThus $\\sec\\theta=OA$, $\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=OB$ and $\\cot\\theta=PB$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q102-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How is $\\sec\\theta$ being the reciprocal of $\\cos\\theta$ demonstrated on this diagram?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$PY=\\cos\\theta$ and $OA=\\sec\\theta=\\frac{1}{PY}$.\n\nAs $\\theta$ approaches $90^\\circ$, $PY$ approaches zero and $OA$ grows without bound. As $\\theta$ approaches $0^\\circ$, $PY$ approaches $1$ from below and $OA$ approaches $1$ from above.",
          "worked": "Since $OP=1$, the projection length is $PY=\\cos\\theta$. In right triangle $OPA$, $\\cos\\theta=\\frac{OP}{OA}=\\frac{1}{OA}$, so $OA=\\frac{1}{PY}$.\n\nAs $\\theta$ approaches $90^\\circ$ from below, $PY$ approaches zero from above and $OA$ grows without bound. Conversely, as $\\theta$ approaches $0^\\circ$ from above, $PY$ approaches $1$ from below and $OA$ approaches $1$ from above.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q102-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Explain similarly for $\\cot\\theta$ and $\\tan\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$PA=\\tan\\theta$ and $PB=\\cot\\theta=\\frac{1}{PA}$ for the acute angles shown.\n\nAs $\\theta$ approaches $90^\\circ$, $PA$ grows without bound and $PB$ approaches zero. As $\\theta$ approaches $0^\\circ$, $PA$ approaches zero and $PB$ grows without bound.",
          "worked": "The right triangles give $PA=\\tan\\theta$ and $PB=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}=\\cot\\theta$. For $0^\\circ<\\theta<90^\\circ$, these lengths are reciprocals.\n\nAs $\\theta$ approaches $90^\\circ$ from below, $PA$ grows without bound while $PB$ approaches zero from above. Conversely, as $\\theta$ approaches $0^\\circ$ from above, $PA$ approaches zero from above while $PB$ grows without bound.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
